{
 "$comment": "A store's books (lib/books.js, owner Value): the chart of accounts every store starts from, and the rules that post business events to it. Each account is a node of the books.account kind placed in the books.chart hierarchy under its group; a store adds its own accounts in its namespace. Entries are journals of the platform's one ledger (lib/wallet.js): they balance in every currency, are written to the kernel's hash-chained log first, cannot be edited or deleted, and are corrected only by a linked reversal. A rule names the record and the change that triggers it and the accounts each part of the amount goes to; the parts are computed in lib/books.js by the measure its record's source names. Each type names its normal side and where it shows: the balance sheet (assets, liabilities, equity) or profit and loss (income, expense).",
